  "description": "Claude Code–style workflow kit for macOS, Linux and Windows, installed whole or as the modules you choose: objective answers (an objection is a reason to check again, not to give in; the user's guess at a cause is one hypothesis; «как думаешь?» gets a verdict, not praise; agreement without a look at anything sends the agent back), facts, not guesses (the agent's final report is held against the conversation — test results and their numbers, CI status, deploys, pushes, checks, files, line numbers, links, versions and prices — questions get looked up with a source for each fact, and fake checks are refused), parallel work (the agent hands independent parts of a task to subagents — explorer, researcher, worker, test-writer, reviewers — in one step and keeps working instead of waiting or polling, plus native Swarm guidance; /parallel), speed, context and quota (commands that failed in the terminal sandbox are remembered per project and run outside it from the start, context budget with targeted reads, a stop to loops of failing commands, and plan-limit hints when quota gets tight), bundled MCP server (antigravity-plus_tools: typed lsp_*, memory_search, git_state, quota tools), an agent that sets up projects on its own (creates a git repository with a safe first commit, writes AGENTS.md with /init, records project rules) and changes settings for you (/settings: MCP servers, plugin options) while its own permissions stay yours to change, several agents on one project without overwriting each other, full access on a single grant (the agent runs every command itself), Bypass Mode switched on once with /bypass and remembered for every conversation (no permission prompts; only system-level actions — sudo, system folders, disks, autostart, keys, the agent's own permissions — still ask), Git and GitHub (/git: the repository's state in one command, branches and syncing, conflicts step by step, history — who changed what and why, safe undo, GitHub issues, pull requests, review threads, releases via /release, and /ci tracking), code navigation through language servers (/lsp: pyright, sourcekit-lsp, kotlin-lsp, typescript-language-server, gopls, rust-analyzer or clangd — def, refs, calls, hover, symbols, find, check, rename; warm background daemons), /deps (dependency vulnerability and outdated audit), /deploy with checks and rollback, /ui-check (headless Chrome screenshots), /mobile (iOS simulator and Android emulator), /context (what fills context), /insights (hook statistics), /claude (Antigravity → Claude Code task hand-off), /standup, /hooks, secret protection, auto-memory shared with Claude Code (/memory, /remember, /handoff), a Stop hook that finishes task.md and checks every edited file, /usage cost dashboard and live side panel, /export, /doctor, /update, 7 subagents, a git-context session hook and a safety guard.",
